LISP> (load "classics")

Classic Lisp programs. Load one, then:
 eliza    (eliza)       DOCTOR, 1966
 deriv    (deriv-demo)  differentiation
 animals  (animals)     it learns
 meval    (meval-demo)  Lisp in Lisp
 queens   (queens 8)    eight queens
 hanoi    (hanoi 4)     Towers of Hanoi
 life     (life 8)      Conway's Life
(load "eliza") loads ELIZA, and so on.
T
LISP> (load "deriv")
T
LISP> (deriv-demo)
d/dx (+ (* 3 (^ X 2)) (* 2 X) 1)
   = (+ (* 6 X) 2)
d/dx (* X (SIN X))
   = (+ (* X (COS X)) (SIN X))
d/dx (/ 1 X)
   = (/ -1 (^ X 2))
d/dx (EXP (* 2 X))
   = (* 2 (EXP (* 2 X)))
d/dx (LOG (^ X 2))
   = (/ (* 2 X) (^ X 2))
d/dx (SIN (COS X))
   = (* (COS (COS X)) (* -1 (SIN X)))
d/dx (* (+ X 1) (- X 1))
   = (+ (+ X 1) (- X 1))
NIL
